# Phase 18 MessageId public API parity — 20261015T015934Z

- Audited the pinned Java 5.5.1 `MessageDecoder.createMessageId` overloads, `decodeMessageId`, and mutable `MessageId` constructor/getter/setter surface against the Common crate. Rust previously generated record IDs only inside the decoder and had no public decoder or `MessageId` type.
- Added public `create_message_id`, `create_message_id_from_host_bytes`, `decode_message_id`, `MessageId`, and typed input errors. Record decoding now shares the public uppercase-hex encoder. Rust preserves Java's IPv4 length selection, signed offset, ignored trailing bytes, invalid-hex nibble conversion, and out-of-range port rejection.
- Expanded the invoked Java 5.5.1 fixture and Rust regression for IPv4/IPv6, both create overload shapes, negative offsets, nullable/mutable fields, invalid hex, trailing bytes, short input, invalid port, unresolved address, and invalid host-byte length. Updated Phase 8 mapping and the current fixture digest: `a79a06ff99f4889c283e749939820e184f6c0f3ab9179d0a8e92af4b4414b53b`.
- PASS: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-common --all-features --locked` (21 unit, 8 message decode, 1 topic validator, 11 doctests); strict Common Clippy; pinned offline Maven `verify` (37 scenarios, fixture drift and Java/Rust cross-decodes); `cargo fmt --all -- --check`; `git diff --check`; fixture SHA-256 verification.
- This closes the MessageId API slice only. Broad P18-V01 source/API/input/error/flow and reverse-export reconciliation remains open. The complete P18-V02 matrix still needs a final-revision rerun after all fixes; current-revision GitHub Ubuntu evidence and Phase 19 Docker/Broker scenarios remain outstanding. No plan changed; no push, release, or tag action taken.

## CRC property helper — 2026-10-15

- Pinned Java `MessageDecoder.createCrc32(ByteBuffer, int)` and `createCrc32(ByteBuf, int)` append the `__CRC32#` property key, separator, ten least-significant-first decimal digits (zeroes for nonpositive inputs), and property terminator. Added public Rust `append_crc32_property` and an invoked Java fixture that compares both buffer overloads for zero, positive, maximum and negative signed inputs.
- Updated the Phase 8 method map and current message fixture SHA-256: `70fa17767b0ec98b9e6b6885572e7dfc61ff43609dfb377e7cfca34c6e9348f5`.
- PASS: Common all-feature tests (21 unit, 9 message decode, 1 topic validator, 11 doctests); strict Common Clippy; pinned offline Maven `verify` (37 scenarios, fixture drift and cross-decodes); formatting, diff and checksum checks.
- This closes the CRC helper slice only; P18-V01 remains open, and current-revision full P18-V02 gates, Ubuntu evidence and Phase 19 local Broker/Docker scenarios remain outstanding.

## Record property extraction — 2026-10-15

- Pinned Java exposes `MessageDecoder.decodeProperties(ByteBuffer)` separately from full record decode. Added public `decode_record_properties`, which reads the record without materializing the body and returns `None` for the Java null result when no property entries exist.
- Extended each of the ten Java-generated message fixtures with a direct call to `decodeProperties`; the Rust message decode regression compares the standalone result for every V1/V2, host and compression case. Fixture SHA-256: `b5f5f89b6e0df7c2e706fd121a91860ea3a4a8f0e923893c9d6c8170704b7744`.
- PASS: Common all-feature tests (21 unit, 9 message decode, 1 topic validator, 11 doctests); strict Common Clippy; pinned offline Maven `verify` (37 scenarios, fixture drift and Java/Rust cross-decodes); format, diff and checksum checks.
- This closes the record-property extraction slice only. P18-V01 still has additional public decoder/encoder methods and the wider bidirectional API audit open; final-revision P18-V02, GitHub Ubuntu evidence and Phase 19 Docker/Broker scenarios also remain outstanding.
